From: avlo-py-build <py-build@avlo.local>
Subject: [PATCH] AVLO: js-bridge closure — no "js" module registration

Delete the one registration that makes the host realm importable from
Python: importhook.register_js_module("js", jsglobals) in
finalizeBootstrap's non-snapshot branch. JsFinder.find_spec resolves
top-level names ONLY from jsfinder.jsproxies, so without it `import js`
exhausts the full meta_path -> ModuleNotFoundError at finder level,
independent of the in-Python harness guard (which stays for pyodide_js/
pyodide/_pyodide coverage). register_js_finder() and the "pyodide_js"
registration stay: webloop does `from pyodide_js._api import
scheduleCallback` at import time and pyodide/__init__ runs
_initialize_event_loop() during boot — removing either breaks boot.

P1 note: this patch's former snapshot half (the getExpectedKeys hiwire
table rewrite in src/js/snapshot.ts) is PARKED in
patches/parked/pyodide/0008b-avlo-expected-keys.reference.patch until
P2's owned-capture rewrite — snapshots are dormant for all of Phase 1
(the client forces cold boots).

diff --git a/src/js/api.ts b/src/js/api.ts
index 8f73e57..6531895 100644
--- a/src/js/api.ts
+++ b/src/js/api.ts
@@ -755,7 +755,6 @@ API.finalizeBootstrap = function (
     syncUpSnapshotLoad2(jsglobals, snapshotConfig, snapshotDeserializer);
   } else {
     importhook.register_js_finder();
-    importhook.register_js_module("js", jsglobals);
     importhook.register_js_module("pyodide_js", pyodide);
     importhook.register_windows_finder();
   }
